WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.640
He’s an international man of mystery with
a license to kill.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:12.120
A lady’s man of legendary proportions known
for his rugged good looks and impossibly smooth

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.120
charm.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.690
He’s a lover of fast cars and adventure
who spends his spare time at cocktail parties

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.250
and in casinos.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.910
I am, of course, talking about the one and
only…

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.190
Rubirosa, Porfirio Rubirosa.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.140
Wait, what?

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.920
While that description might have sounded
strikingly similar to everyone’s favourite

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:40.070
secret agent James Bond, Porfirio Rubirosa
was very much a living, breathing man.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:45.570
And his life was so remarkable it’s going
to be quite a challenge to cover it in a single

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.570
YouTube video.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:48.920
But let me just give you a few highlights
to whet your whistle.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:54.909
Porfirio Rubirosa was a man so suave he inspired
Ralph Lauren to create the now world famous

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:57.109
Polo fashion brand.

00:00:57.109 --> 00:01:02.579
He was so successful that despite being born
to a modest family in the Dominican Republic

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:09.070
he amassed an incredible fortune and ended
up living among world leaders and movie stars.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:14.420
And he was so charismatic that some of the
most lusted-after women in all of history

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.510
cheated on their husbands just to spend a
single night with him.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:20.840
Intrigued?

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.439
You should be.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:27.930
Rubirosa was born in the Dominican Republic
in 1909, but he was to spend his formative

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:33.400
years in Paris, where he lived until failing
the international baccalaureate at the age

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.570
of 17.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:39.549
With no real prospects in Europe, he went
home, where he was to find the country of

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:43.370
his birth on the cusp of great change.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:50.619
Because a few years later in 1930, a man named
Rafael Trujillo helped stage a military coup,

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:56.259
overthrowing the government of the Dominican
Republic and installing himself as generalissimo.

00:01:56.259 --> 00:02:00.859
Rubirosa, meanwhile, had joined the military,
though he spent most of his time playing his

00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:02.969
favourite sport - polo.

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:08.030
He was one of those guys who was good at everything
– well, apart from the international baccalaureate

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.970
exams - and before long he was captain of
the national polo team.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:19.810
And it was at a polo game the young Rubirosa
would catch the eye of General Trujillo himself.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:25.030
As we’ll come to see, Rubi, as Rubirosa
was sometimes known, possessed the kind of

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:30.520
charm that would make Hugh Grant look like
a football hooligan eight pints down on derby

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.460
day, and Trujillo was immediately impressed
with the boy.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:39.920
So impressed, in fact, that he hired Rubi
to be a lieutenant in his own personal guard

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.700
on the spot.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:47.290
It was a huge promotion - more money and status,
not to mention the backing of the nation’s

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.290
new ruler.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:55.480
But there was one teeny tiny catch - Trujillo
just so happened to be one of the most brutal

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.630
dictators in modern history.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:03.370
Three weeks after rising to power, he renamed
the Dominican capital ‘Trujillo city’

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:09.670
in his own honour, and churches were soon
required to display the slogan ‘God in heaven,

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.090
Trujillo on earth’ on their premises.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:17.880
To say he had a bit of an ego would be the
understatement of the century.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.860
Trujillo would eventually be assassinated
by a CIA-sponsored hit team some 30 years

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:29.680
later, but in the intervening years he ruled
the Dominican Republic with an iron fist.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:36.760
Political assassinations, widespread oppression,
blatant corruption - you name it, Trujillo

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:43.030
was either doing it, ordering it, or turning
a blind eye to it, and, thanks to a certain

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:48.120
penchant for murdering people who ticked him
off, those that got in his bad books didn’t

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.160
stay there for long.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:56.640
Trujillo was an all-round bad guy, but his
most infamous and evil act was to order the

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.290
killing of Haitians living in the Dominican
Republic’s north-western frontier in a slaughter

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.820
known today as the Parsley massacre.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:10.070
It’s thought to have led to the deaths of
as many as 35,000 Haitians.

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:16.489
OK, so what would you do if you found yourself
working under the watchful eye of quite literally

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:20.140
the scariest and most powerful man in your
entire country?

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.920
Keep your head down and try to stay out of
trouble?

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.430
Perhaps even attempt an escape to safety in
some far-off country?

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.670
Yeah - Me too.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.210
But not Rubirosa.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.150
No, he seduced his murderous new boss’ daughter.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:40.850
To give you an idea of how the generalissimo
felt about his little girl, I can tell you

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:47.310
he’d named her Flor de Oro, which means
Flower of Gold, so I think it’s safe to

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.430
assume she was rather important to him.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:57.220
It’s also safe to assume Trujillo had had
men killed for far, far less serious crimes

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:00.350
than deflowering his precious Golden Flower.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:06.510
And no doubt he would have had Rubirosa killed,
too - if he’d been able to find him.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:12.510
You see, once the hormones had worn off a
bit, young Rubi had realised the precariousness

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.810
of his situation and gone into hiding.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.650
And it seems the move paid off, because - given
a little time to cool down - the generalissimo

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:28.210
decided against brutally murdering Rubirosa,
and instead presented him with two options.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:34.510
The details were complicated, but it pretty
much boiled down to this: marriage or death.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:40.270
After considering the offer for a good nanosecond,
Rubi decided marriage was the way forward.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:46.280
The wedding day was declared a national holiday,
and - now well and truly established in Trujillo’s

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:52.620
inner circle - Rubirosa was given another
promotion, this time to the position of diplomat

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.490
to the Dominican Republic.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:06:00.210
His first post was in Berlin during the 1936
Olympics, where he would find himself watching

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:05.990
the Games alongside Hitler himself in the
Führer’s private box.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:10.669
Rubirosa had officially hit the big time,
and his new career would see him stationed

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:17.360
all over the world - in Germany, France, Italy,
Belgium, the United States, and Argentina.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.480
He would eventually obtain the position of
‘Inspector of Embassies’, which seems

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.590
to have been a job invented just for him and
gave him the excuse to travel pretty much

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.310
anywhere he wanted on official business.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.639
On the surface it seemed like the perfect
role.

00:06:33.639 --> 00:06:38.930
There weren’t many duties to attend to,
aside from rubbing shoulders with world leaders

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:43.150
and making friends with some of the most famous
people alive at the time.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:50.240
But some people believe Rubirosa’s unusual
job was in fact nothing more than a front.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:54.900
That instead of a diplomat, he was in fact
a spy.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:59.740
A hit man and an enforcer carrying out Trujillo’s
will around the world.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:04.650
It’s a big claim, and it’s never been
proven for sure.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:10.060
But we do know in the 60s Rubirosa was questioned
by the New York district attorney about two

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:18.990
missing men, anti-Trujillo exile Sergio Bencosme,
who disappeared in 1935, and Spanish politician

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:26.490
and writer Jesus Galindez, who suffered the
same fate in 1956 after writing a none-too-flattering

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.670
book about the Trujillo regime.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:35.070
Rubirosa was also kept under surveillance
by the FBI for some three decades, so it seems

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:38.640
the Americans were more than a little suspicious
about him.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:43.449
Whether or not Rubi really was busy bumping
people off on behalf of his boss, what he

00:07:43.449 --> 00:07:49.180
most certainly was busy doing was taking the
emerging international jet-set scene of the

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.919
40s and 50s by storm.

00:07:51.919 --> 00:07:57.370
He was known to be fast friends with the likes
of Frank Sinatra and the Kennedys, but the

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:04.610
thing that defined Porfirio Rubirosa above
all else was his reputation as perhaps the

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:09.020
greatest playboy and womaniser since Casanova
himself.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:15.949
Or, to offer you a more recent comparison,
Rubirosa was to the world’s most recognisable

00:08:15.949 --> 00:08:19.080
women what Ash Ketchum is to Pokemon.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:27.070
And just one look at Rubi’s poked-dex is
enough to tell you he pretty much did catch

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:28.460
’em all.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:35.520
In his life, he was linked with film stars
and singers including Zsa Zsa Gabor, Ava Gardner,

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.599
Jayne Mansfield, Veronica Lake, Dolores Del
Rio, Eartha Kitt, Marilyn Monroe, Maria Montez,

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:48.620
Rita Hayworth, Dorothy Dandridge, Lupe Vélez,
Judy Garland, Peggy Hopkins Joyce, Joan Crawford,

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:54.820
and Kim Novak, as well as the Queen Consort
of Iran, Soraya Esfandiary, the First Lady

00:08:54.820 --> 00:09:00.529
of Argentina, Eva Perón (better known as
Evita) and dozens of others.

00:09:00.529 --> 00:09:06.130
It’s claimed Rubirosa was so irresistible
to women that all it took was one slow dance

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:08.129
and they were his.

00:09:08.129 --> 00:09:13.069
In fact, some say he didn’t even need to
bother lacing up his dancing shoes, and as

00:09:13.069 --> 00:09:19.449
his unrivalled reputation as the ultimate
gentleman and lover grew, women would simply

00:09:19.449 --> 00:09:24.829
grab hold of him at parties, drag him to the
nearest deserted corner, and have their wicked

00:09:24.829 --> 00:09:26.680
way with him.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:31.430
You might be wondering how any man, no matter
how good looking or charming, could have such

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.579
an effect on women.

00:09:32.579 --> 00:09:37.500
But it wasn’t just Rubi’s charm that attracted
the ladies.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:43.730
No, God had bestowed Porfirio Rubirosa with
another ‘gift’.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:50.209
I’m not sure quite how to put this, so I’ll
let Truman Capote tell you about Rubi’s

00:09:50.209 --> 00:09:53.209
special erm… asset.

00:09:53.209 --> 00:09:59.550
In his unfinished novel ‘Answered Prayers’,
the legendary writer described a certain part

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:06.420
of Rubirosa’s anatomy as ‘An eleven-inch
café-au-lait sinker as thick as a man’s

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.420
wrist.’

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:13.300
Yes, Rubirosa’s pork soldier was said to
be so enormous he had to have his underwear

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.879
specially tailored just to accommodate it.

00:10:16.879 --> 00:10:19.579
But let’s not forget, Rubirosa was a married
man.

00:10:19.579 --> 00:10:24.220
And while not all of his Hollywood liaisons
came during his marriage with Trujillo’s

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.679
daughter Flor, at least some of them did.

00:10:27.679 --> 00:10:32.610
After one too many nights coming home late
from ‘work’ with whiskey on his breath

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:38.600
and lipstick on his collar, Flor filed for
divorce in 1938.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:43.639
It seems unlikely Rubirosa was too gutted
at this turn of events from a romantic point

00:10:43.639 --> 00:10:49.779
of view, but the divorce had put him in a
bit of a tight spot - he was broke.

00:10:49.779 --> 00:10:56.119
While he made a reasonable income in his capacity
as a diplomat, he’d largely relied on Flor’s

00:10:56.119 --> 00:11:03.319
riches to finance his extravagant lifestyle
of polo playing and parties.

00:11:03.319 --> 00:11:10.649
Luckily, this was Europe just before the beginning
of World War 2, and that created certain opportunities

00:11:10.649 --> 00:11:14.670
for a man with diplomatic immunity and friends
in high places.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:21.449
It’s thought Rubirosa began discreetly selling
Dominican visas to Jews desperate to get out

00:11:21.449 --> 00:11:23.689
of Europe before it was too late.

00:11:23.689 --> 00:11:29.149
And when a jeweller asked him to use his diplomatic
passport to help recover hundreds of thousands

00:11:29.149 --> 00:11:37.019
of dollars in rare gemstones from Madrid,
Rubirosa was happy to oblige – for a price.

00:11:37.019 --> 00:11:41.889
By some estimations, he made close to half
a million dollars from these schemes and others

00:11:41.889 --> 00:11:46.170
like them - that’s more like 7 million in
today’s money.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:52.149
But living on the wrong side of the law is
a risky business and, let’s face it, a bit

00:11:52.149 --> 00:11:55.490
too much like hard work for a gentleman of
leisure.

00:11:55.490 --> 00:12:00.750
So as war descended over Europe, Rubirosa
came up with another way to get his hands

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:06.360
on some fast cash – he found the richest
woman he could and married her.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:11.870
Rubi was back living in Paris at the time,
and the lucky lady turned out to be Danielle

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:17.339
Darrieux, France’s leading film star, who
fell for Rubi’s charms after he was asked

00:12:17.339 --> 00:12:19.889
to escort her home from a cocktail party.

00:12:19.889 --> 00:12:25.339
But before they could get married, Rubirosa
was imprisoned by the gestapo, who’d gotten

00:12:25.339 --> 00:12:31.369
wind of his antics spiriting Jews out of Europe
and suspected he was a spy.

00:12:31.369 --> 00:12:37.699
Darrieux offered to play a series of concerts
for the Nazis if Rubirosa was released, and

00:12:37.699 --> 00:12:39.540
a deal was struck.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.019
They were married soon after.

00:12:42.019 --> 00:12:47.860
But the agreement had an unfortunate side-effect
- playing concerts for the Nazis meant Darrieux

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:53.259
was viewed as a sympathiser by her fellow
countrymen, and Rubirosa himself was thought

00:12:53.259 --> 00:12:56.179
by some to be a German agent.

00:12:56.179 --> 00:13:03.439
It made the couple a target, and in 1944 the
French resistance took aim - literally.

00:13:03.439 --> 00:13:09.269
The couple were ambushed while driving along
the Boulevard Malesherbes in Paris, and Rubirosa

00:13:09.269 --> 00:13:13.389
was shot 3 times while trying to shield his
wife.

00:13:13.389 --> 00:13:18.489
He made a full recovery, but decided it would
be a wise move to wait out the rest of the

00:13:18.489 --> 00:13:21.839
war on a small farm in the countryside.

00:13:21.839 --> 00:13:27.410
When the war ended, Generalissimo Trujillo,
who seemed to have gotten over Rubirosa’s

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:33.430
divorce from his daughter, sent his young
diplomat a new assignment - a posting in Italy.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:38.110
Rubirosa and Darrieux moved to Rome, where
the local press clamoured to catch a glimpse

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.519
of the glamorous couple.

00:13:39.519 --> 00:13:45.070
An interview with a local newspaper was arranged
for the day after their arrival, and when

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:51.779
a gangly, enthusiastic reporter turned up,
Rubirosa’s life was about to change once

00:13:51.779 --> 00:13:52.779
again.

00:13:52.779 --> 00:13:57.759
You see, the journalist wasn’t just any
old hack - she just so happened to be the

00:13:57.759 --> 00:14:00.589
single richest girl in the world.

00:14:00.589 --> 00:14:07.119
Her name was Doris Duke, and, despite her
unfathomable riches, she’d decided to try

00:14:07.119 --> 00:14:08.920
her hand at a ‘normal’ job.

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:13.999
The unusual career choice wasn’t to last,
but it did put her in the same room as Rubirosa

00:14:13.999 --> 00:14:19.269
for an hour or two on one fateful day in 1947.

00:14:19.269 --> 00:14:24.620
And when Porfirio Rubirosa was concerned,
an hour or two was more than enough.

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:29.600
Doris’ father was James Buchanan Duke - he’s
the reason Duke University in North Carolina

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:30.970
has its name.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:35.489
He was also the owner of American Tobacco
and the man who first invented the mass produced

00:14:35.489 --> 00:14:36.489
cigarette.

00:14:36.489 --> 00:14:43.790
And, as the estimated 100 million people who
died from tobacco-related causes in the twentieth

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:47.660
can attest to - those little cancer sticks
really caught on.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:52.820
Doris Duke was James’ only daughter and
heir, which meant she was to inherit the entirety

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.480
of his fortune.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.230
In today’s money, her net worth would have
been measured in the billions.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:04.540
She fell for Rubirosa hard, and while he was
already married to an extravagantly wealthy

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:10.610
film star, the pull of the richest girl in
the world was just too much for him.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:16.449
It’s reported Doris Duke paid Darrieux a
cool 1 million dollars to divorce Rubirosa,

00:15:16.449 --> 00:15:22.380
and before long, he was walking down the aisle
for the third time in 15 years.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:29.069
On their wedding day Doris Duke gave Rubi
a full stable of polo horses, a 17th century

00:15:29.069 --> 00:15:37.370
Parisian hotel, 500,000 dollars in cash, and
a converted B-25 bomber.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:42.810
You know you’ve married rich when 500 grand
is the least interesting part of your wedding

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:43.810
gift.

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:48.319
If Rubirosa had been living the high life
up until this point, he was now ready to go

00:15:48.319 --> 00:15:51.809
the playboy equivalent of super-saiyan.

00:15:51.809 --> 00:15:57.819
He had the resources to do quite literally
anything he wanted, anywhere he wanted.

00:15:57.819 --> 00:16:05.330
Unfortunately, it seems what he most wanted
to do was his ex-wife, Flor de Oro - and when

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:10.149
Doris Duke found out the marriage was over
before it had really begun.

00:16:10.149 --> 00:16:16.209
But the great thing about marrying rich is
that even being a divorcee can be pretty well

00:16:16.209 --> 00:16:22.029
paid - and that’s despite the fact Duke’s
lawyers had gotten Rubirosa drunk and forced

00:16:22.029 --> 00:16:25.720
him to sign a prenuptial agreement on the
night before the wedding.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:33.149
As part of the divorce settlement he was given
$25,000 per year until he next married - the

00:16:33.149 --> 00:16:37.199
equivalent of close to 300 grand today.

00:16:37.199 --> 00:16:40.649
And Rubirosa made the most of it.

00:16:40.649 --> 00:16:45.689
When he wasn’t spending his days playing
polo or boxing, he was indulging one of his

00:16:45.689 --> 00:16:48.269
other great passions - fast cars.

00:16:48.269 --> 00:16:53.779
He entered his first competitive race in Le
Mans in 1950 behind the wheel of his very

00:16:53.779 --> 00:17:01.859
own Ferrari 166 MM, one of just 47 made, and
he drove in the Reims 12 Hour Race 3 years

00:17:01.859 --> 00:17:02.859
later.

00:17:02.859 --> 00:17:08.439
He even managed to get himself a seat in the
1955 Formula 1 Grand Prix in Bordeaux where

00:17:08.439 --> 00:17:13.929
he was due to race alongside the likes of
F1 legend Stirling Moss, but he fell ill in

00:17:13.929 --> 00:17:16.490
the buildup and had to pull out.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:22.039
To most people, this kind of hedonistic life
would have been a dream come true.

00:17:22.039 --> 00:17:24.809
But Rubirosa wasn’t most people.

00:17:24.809 --> 00:17:30.920
He once said that most men’s ambition was
to save money, while his was to spend it.

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:36.789
And that wasn’t just a pithy catchphrase
he dreamed up to look good in print - he really

00:17:36.789 --> 00:17:37.789
meant it.

00:17:37.789 --> 00:17:44.879
It’s estimated that during his lifetime,
Rubirosa spent as much as 100 million dollars

00:17:44.879 --> 00:17:48.480
- the equivalent or upwards north of a billion
dollars in today’s money.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:54.169
And a desire for more money was probably the
motivating factor behind Rubirosa’s fourth

00:17:54.169 --> 00:17:55.169
marriage, too.

00:17:55.169 --> 00:18:00.899
But of course, when you’ve already divorced
the richest woman in the world, the only way

00:18:00.899 --> 00:18:03.870
is down - in financial terms at least.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:10.280
Still, Rubi was a man of principles - dubious
principles, but principles all the same - and

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:14.539
he didn’t want to fall too far down the
financial pecking order.

00:18:14.539 --> 00:18:21.070
So he took the only logical course of action
available to him - he married the second richest

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.480
woman in the world.

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:23.480
Seriously.

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:29.510
Her name was Barbara Hutton, another heiress
this time set to inherit retail tycoon Frank

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.559
Winfield Woolworth’s estate.

00:18:31.559 --> 00:18:36.070
On the wedding present list for this one was
the largest coffee plantation in the Dominican

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:44.070
Republic, 2.5 million dollars in cash, and
yet another B-25 bomber, because Rubi had

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.250
managed to crash the first one.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:51.399
Now, you might think I’m being very cynical
here, claiming he was only after financial

00:18:51.399 --> 00:18:55.389
gain in his pursuit of these unbelievably
wealthy women.

00:18:55.389 --> 00:19:00.230
After all, perhaps it was just a coincidence
he got hitched to the two richest women in

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:03.019
the world, one after the other.

00:19:03.019 --> 00:19:06.590
And hey, maybe you’re right.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.710
Maybe… but probably not.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:15.309
Because marriage number 4 was to last a grand
total of 53 days, during which time Rubi took

00:19:15.309 --> 00:19:20.210
a string of lovers and by accounts hardly
even saw his new wife.

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:26.940
It’s thought the whole affair cost Barbara
Hutton $66,000 per day.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:32.040
Another marriage soon followed, but it seems
Rubirosa may finally have decided he had enough

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:36.299
money to be getting along with, because he
didn’t bother hunting down the world’s

00:19:36.299 --> 00:19:42.940
third richest woman, but instead opted for
youth and beauty in the form of Odile Rodin,

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:46.410
who was a full 31 years his junior.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:52.090
It was to be his last marriage, and though
it’s said he remained one randy bugger until

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:58.019
his dying day, rumour has it Rodin was even
more unfaithful than he was.

00:19:58.019 --> 00:20:02.539
Though the years were finally beginning to
catch up with Rubirosa, they would never quite

00:20:02.539 --> 00:20:04.620
have the chance to overtake him.

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:11.600
Because he died in 1965 at the age of 56 in
much the same way he’d lived - fast and

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.580
at great cost.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:19.169
After pulling an all-nighter to celebrate
winning the Coup de France Polo Cup, Rubirosa

00:20:19.169 --> 00:20:23.690
unwisely opted to drive his Ferrari home at
8am.

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:30.050
No doubt wildly over the limit, he hit a tree
at around 80 miles per hour, and though he

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:34.650
survived the crash, the wooden steering wheel
had crushed his torso, and he died on the

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:36.519
way to hospital.

00:20:36.519 --> 00:20:41.520
His death signalled the end of an era - he
was the last and perhaps the greatest of the

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:46.279
jet set playboys - but his legacy lives on
to this day.

00:20:46.279 --> 00:20:51.370
I mentioned his similarities to James Bond
at the start of this video, and many people

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:58.340
believe Rubirosa was in fact the real-life
inspiration for double oh seven.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:05.260
While Ian Fleming never explicitly named Rubirosa
as the basis for his books, the two did likely

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:10.960
know each other - they moved in the same circles
and had many mutual friends, including Errol

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:15.909
Flynn and Noel Coward, who lived near Fleming
on the north shore of Jamaica.

00:21:15.909 --> 00:21:21.550
Which is, of course, not far from the Dominican
Republic where Rubirosa was born.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:27.710
Much like the rumours he was a real life spy
and hitman, we’ll likely never know whether

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:30.970
Rubirosa really was the inspiration for Bond.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:37.470
But there is another way Rubi’s legacy is
remembered around the world.

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:44.380
Because it turns out the frankly frightening
size of his greatest asset led Parisian waiters

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:50.630
to jokingly call the large pepper mills they
offered to their customers ‘Rubirosa’s’.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:55.929
The name spread around the world, and in some
restaurants it’s still in use today.

00:21:55.929 --> 00:22:01.639
Something to think about the next time you
grind a little pepper on your spaghetti bolognaise.

00:22:01.639 --> 00:22:12.309
Thanks for watching.

